content=\"offense\"><h4>Offense</h4><hr /><strong>Speed</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"speed\">  <li>Land 50 ft</li>  </ul><br />  <strong>Melee</strong> 2 hooves -2 (1d4+1)<br />   <ul class=\"sbcSemicolonList\">  <li><strong>Space</strong> 10 ft</li>   <li><strong>Reach</strong> 5 ft</li>  </ul> <br />  </div></div>    <div class=\"sbcSection\" data-content=\"statistics\"><h4>Statistics</h4><hr /><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"attributes\"><li><strong>Str</strong> 16</li><li><strong>Dex</strong> 14</li><li><strong>Con</strong> 17</li><li><strong>Int</strong> 2</li><li><strong>Wis</strong> 13</li><li><strong>Cha</strong> 7</li></ul><br /><ul class=\"sbcSemicolonList\" data-content=\"base-attack\"><li><strong>Base Atk</strong>+1</li><li><strong>CMB</strong> +5</li><li><strong>CMD</strong> 17  (21 vs. trip) </li></ul><br />  <strong>Feats</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"feats\">  <li>Endurance</li>  <li>Run</li>  </ul><br />   <strong>Skills</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"skills\">  <li>Perception +6</li>  </ul>  <br />    <strong>SQ</strong><ul class=\"sbcCommaList\" data-content=\"sq\">  <li>docile</li>  </ul><br />   </div>  <div class=\"sbcSection\" data-content=\"ecology\"><h4>Ecology</h4><hr />  <strong>Environment</strong>   temperate plains <br />   <strong>Organization</strong>  solitary, pair, or herd (3-30)<br />   <strong>Treasure</strong>  none   <br />  </div>    <div class=\"sbcSection\" data-content=\"special-abilities\"><h4> Special Abilities </h4><hr />  <p><strong>Docile (Ex)</strong> Unless specifically trained for combat (see the Handle Animal skill on page 97 of the Pathfinder RPG Core Rulebook), a horse's hooves are treated as secondary attacks.  Horses stand 5 to 6 feet tall at the shoulder and weigh between 1,000 and 1,500 pounds.    </p>  </div>    <div class=\"sbcSection\" data-content=\"description\"><h4> Description </h4><hr /><div class=\"sbcPreWrap\">\nThe statistics above are for a typical riding horse, called by some a \"light horse.\" Some horses are larger and heartier, bred for labor such as pulling plows or carriages. These horses are called \"heavy horses\" and gain the following adjustments to the base statistics detailed above.\n\nHeavy Horse: A heavy horse gains the advanced simple template. In addition, it also gains a bite attack that inf licts 1d4 damage, and its hoof damage increases to 1d6. As with a light horse, a heavy horse can be specifically trained for combat with the Handle Animal skill.\n</div></div>  </div><hr class=\"sbcBorder\" /></div><p></p></div><br /><hr /><div class=\"rawInputContainer\" style=\"margin-top:15px\"><h2 style=\"text-align:middle;border:none;text-transform:uppercase;color:#000\">RAW INPUT</h2><hr /><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:14px\">    Horse (CR 1)\nSource PFRPG Bestiary \nCR 1 \nXP 400 \nN Large animal  \nInit +2; Senses low-light vision, scent; Perception +6   \nDefense   \nAC 11, touch 11, flat-footed 9 (+2 Dex, -1 size)\n\nhp 15 (2d8+6)\n\nFort +6, Ref +5, Will +1   \nOffense   \nSpd 50 ft. \nMelee 2 hooves -2 (1d4+1)\n\nSpace 10 ft.; Reach 5 ft.   \nStatistics   \nStr 16, Dex 14, Con 17, Int 2, Wis 13, Cha 7 \nBase Atk +1; CMB +5; CMD 17 (21 vs. trip)\n\nFeats Endurance, Run \nSkills Perception +6 \nSQ docile   \nEcology   \nEnvironment  temperate plains \nOrganization solitary, pair, or herd (3-30)\n\nTreasure none   \nSpecial abilities   \nDocile (Ex) Unless specifically trained for combat (see the Handle Animal skill on page 97 of the Pathfinder RPG Core Rulebook), a horse's hooves are treated as secondary attacks.  Horses stand 5 to 6 feet tall at the shoulder and weigh between 1,000 and 1,500 pounds.   \nDescription\n\nThe statistics above are for a typical riding horse, called by some a \"light horse.\" Some horses are larger and heartier, bred for labor such as pulling plows or carriages. These horses are called \"heavy horses\" and gain the following adjustments to the base statistics detailed above.\n\nHeavy Horse: A heavy horse gains the advanced simple template. In addition, it also gains a bite attack that inf licts 1d4 damage, and its hoof damage increases to 1d6. As with a light horse, a heavy horse can be specifically trained for combat with the Handle Animal skill.\n    </pre></div>"},"cr":{"base":1},"xp":{"value":0}},"skills":{"acr":{"ability":"dex","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":0},"apr":{"ability":"int","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"art":{"ability":"int","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"blf":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"clm":{"ability":"str","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":0},"crf":{"ability":"int","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"dip":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"dev":{"ability":"dex","rt":true,"acp":true,"rank":0},"dis":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"esc":{"ability":"dex","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":0},"fly":{"ability":"dex","rt":false,"acp":true,"rank":0},"han":{"ability":"cha","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"hea":{"ability":"wis","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"int":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kar":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kdu":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"ken":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kge":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"khi":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"klo":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kna":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kno":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kpl":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"kre":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"lin":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"lor":{"ability":"int","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"per":{"ability":"wis","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":2},"prf":{"ability":"cha","rt":false,"acp":false,"rank":0},"pro":{"ability":"wis","rt":true,"acp":false,"rank":0},"rid":{"abi